{"base_rate":0.38753799392097266,"brier":0.24933799392097267,"bss":-0.05049749622926103,"bss_hi":0.08087288537553616,"bss_lo":-0.22535425903694012,"chart":{"base":[564.5,81.2],"fp":[147.2,219.5],"lead":"62,232.7 272,223.8 482,213.9 692,184.6","note":{"base":"skill -0.05 — higher than 9% of cities","fp":"low end -5pp, high end +34pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 29% of cities","rel":"promised 7% → rained 1%; promised 99% → rained 72%"},"rel":"103.9,462.7 374.9,412.8 568.8,311 682.7,157"},"country":"VN","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.2837082066869301,"ess":314.8850522489777,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Ho Chi Minh City</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Ho Chi Minh City rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>75%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 658 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 21.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.05, ranked 194 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(176&ndash;201) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>74%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>54</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>213</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Ho Chi Minh City</b> <span class=\"muted\">Vietnam</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.05</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>176&ndash;201\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>658 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Ho Chi Minh City &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Ho Chi Minh City\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.82709677419355,370.258064516129 101.36500000000001,307.05882352941177 194.75292307692308,197.20000000000002 272.90523076923074,118.80000000000001 320.65639344262286,71.7049180327869 362.086,44.0 392.1366666666666